  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is six percent (6%) on the total gifts exceeding Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Pesos (₱250,000).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe applicable provisions are found in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) Section 99, which states that the tax for each calendar year shall be six percent (6%) computed on the basis of the total gifts in excess of ₱250,000.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 99 of the NIRC, the donor's tax applies to the total value of gifts made in a calendar year that exceed the exemption threshold of ₱250,000. This means that any amount gifted above this threshold is subject to the 6% tax rate.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts should be aware that only the portion of their total gifts that exceeds ₱250,000 will be taxed at 6%. This exemption allows for a significant amount of gifting without incurring tax liability, which can be beneficial for estate planning and charitable contributions.",
